    {
      "id": "e212",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1374,
      "y": 888,
      "width": 511.9999999999999,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786538392024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. Mount fixtures at least 8'-6\" AFF and clear of cable tray,\ncontainment and the suppression nozzle spray pattern. Coordinate the\nreflected ceiling plan with T-401 and FP-501 before ordering.",
      "originalText": "1. Mount fixtures at least 8'-6\" AFF and clear of cable tray, containment and the suppression nozzle spray pattern. Coordinate the reflected ceiling plan with T-401 and FP-501 before ordering.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 310,
      "versionNonce": 1515169133,
      "index": "b2P",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e213",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1374,
      "y": 953,
      "width": 493,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786538392024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. Lighting is house load, not UPS load. Egress lighting and exit\nsigns carry their own battery so they survive both a utility loss and\nthe EPO.",
      "originalText": "2. Lighting is house load, not UPS load. Egress lighting and exit signs carry their own battery so they survive both a utility loss and the EPO.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 298,
      "versionNonce": 1030909901,
      "index": "b2Q",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e214",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1376,
      "y": 1005,
      "width": 488,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786538392024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Specify 4000 K and CRI 80 or better. Color-coded patch cords are\nonly useful if the colors are distinguishable under the room's light.",
      "originalText": "3. Specify 4000 K and CRI 80 or better. Color-coded patch cords are only useful if the colors are distinguishable under the room's light.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 302,
      "versionNonce": 445443629,
      "index": "b2R",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e215",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1374,
      "y": 1053,
      "width": 490,
      "height": 45,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786538392024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Ask for the calculation in the vertical plane at the rack face,\nwith racks modeled as obstructions. A horizontal-only calc will look\nfine and tell you nothing about the face.",
      "originalText": "4. Ask for the calculation in the vertical plane at the rack face, with racks modeled as obstructions. A horizontal-only calc will look fine and tell you nothing about the face.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 292,
      "versionNonce": 1082695821,
      "index": "b2S",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "seed": 1,
      "autoResize": false
    },
    {
      "id": "e216",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1374,
      "y": 1118,
      "width": 482.00000000000006,
      "height": 30,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786538392024,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5. Lighting contributes about 1.0 W/sq ft to the heat load - already\ncarried in the M-300 calculation. Do not count it twice.",
      "originalText": "5. Lighting contributes about 1.0 W/sq ft to the heat load - already carried in the M-300 calculation. Do not count it twice.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "version": 277,
      "versionNonce": 1696532205,
